// Stage configuration of the Cupmark app: the dev stage (M2-T9, ADR 0023).
//
// Not secrets: the Cognito app client is public and has no secret (infra/src/identity.ts).
// The values reach the app through the CupmarkStage... keys of Config/Info.plist and are
// checked by StageConfig (Cupmark/Configuration/StageConfig.swift). A missing, malformed
// or non-eu-central-1 value shows the "not configured" screen.
//
// "//" starts a comment in an xcconfig file, so every URL writes "/$()/" for "//". $() expands
// to nothing, which leaves "https://..." in the built Info.plist.
//
// PLACEHOLDER values fail StageConfig on purpose (uppercase letters and hyphens are not
// valid in a Cognito app client id or an API Gateway id), so the app shows "not configured"
// instead of calling a wrong host. They are replaced with the outputs AppClientId
// (IdentityAppClientId...) and ApiUrl of the stack cupmark-dev-core: dev in M2-T10, prod in M6.

CUPMARK_STAGE = dev
CUPMARK_HOSTED_DOMAIN = https:/$()/cupmark-dev.auth.eu-central-1.amazoncognito.com
CUPMARK_APP_CLIENT_ID = PLACEHOLDER-SET-IN-M2-T10
CUPMARK_API_URL = https:/$()/PLACEHOLDER-SET-IN-M2-T10.execute-api.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com
CUPMARK_REDIRECT_URL = cupmark:/$()/auth
CUPMARK_SIGN_OUT_URL = cupmark:/$()/signout
